  "title": "Turku, a Golden Autumn",
  "date": "2026-10-25T22:00:00.000Z",
  "content": "Turku, a Golden Autumn\n\nTurku is the old capital of Finland. After a great fire in 1827. Finland moved its capital into Helsinki. Compared with Helsinki and Tampere, Turku has more hills in the city.\n\nThe Turku Cathedral is an obvious landmark in the city.\n\nTurku Cathedral\n\nTurku Cathedral\n\nAutumn in Turku is in a gold filter. Although the city looks bigger than Tampere. There are not so many people on the street.\n\nautumn\n\nThe ferries crossing the river is free of charge. It took about 1 minute to cross.\n\nferry\n\nFunicular is an elevator to climb the mountain. Although it is free. I did not figure out how to use it.\n\nelevator\n\nTurku Castle, only this one building left. It is next to the harbour. The ferries are going to Stockholm.\n\nTurku Castle\n\nIt is about Halloween. There are already decorations on the local families.\n\nHalloween",
